E("es-u2-cr-q12",2,["EA12.2.7"],2,"var",varset([function(){return textq("An organism dies with 28 kg of carbon-14 in its body. Given that the half-life of carbon-14 is 5,730 years, calculate the mass of carbon-14 remaining if the fossil of this organism is 22,920 years old. Show your workings.",["22,920 / 5,730 = 4 half-lives; 28 to 14 to 7 to 3.5 to 1.75 kg remaining."],"<b>Model answer:</b> Number of half-lives = 22,920 / 5,730 = 4. Halving the mass four times: 28 kg, 14 kg, 7 kg, 3.5 kg, 1.75 kg. So 1.75 kg of carbon-14 remains.<br><br><b>Marking points (2 marks):</b><br>- 1 mark: determining that 4 half-lives have passed.<br>- 1 mark: the remaining mass, 1.75 kg.<br><br>The scheme's worked lines contain unit typos from the source document (a gram chain and two values belonging to other items); the banked calculation follows the item's own data.",{});}]),["Divide the age by the half-life first."]);

/* ----- Constructed-Response Practice ----- */
